    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `contactPreference` field is a **derived, read-only** response field on the owner \u2014 the same pattern the codebase already uses for `displayName`, `initials`, `membershipLevel`, and `locality` (computed at DTO-mapping time, not persisted). I followed that existing convention:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `contactPreference` property to the `Owner` response schema as a read-only string enum (`EMAIL` / `PHONE`). The OpenAPI generator produces `OwnerDto` with a nested `ContactPreferenceEnum` from this.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   (owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank())\n       ? OwnerDto.ContactPreferenceEnum.EMAIL : OwnerDto.ContactPreferenceEnum.PHONE\n   ```\n   Returns `EMAIL` when an email is present (non-null, non-blank), otherwise `PHONE`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `AcceptanceTest` (the two new checkpoints: `PHONE` when no email, `EMAIL` when present) \u2014 **2/2 pass**.\n- Full `mvn test` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, no failures or errors.",
